# Fixtures must arrive from a checkout byte for byte.
#
# A PDF is ASCII enough that Git classifies it as text — no NUL byte in the first 8 KiB is the
# whole test — so `core.autocrlf=true`, the Git for Windows default the CI runners keep, rewrites
# every LF in one on checkout. Most of the suite survives that, because the reader rebuilds a
# broken xref by scanning rather than trusting its offsets (DESIGN.md §3.1, recovery is
# first-class). A signature does not survive it: a detached CMS covers a byte range (§12.8.1), so
# `corpus/valid/signed-openssl-cms.pdf` verified on Linux and macOS and failed on Windows alone.
#
# Marking the fixture formats binary settles it for every platform and every future fixture. The
# `-text` is what disables end-of-line conversion; `-diff` keeps `git diff` from printing a
# mangled PDF at review time.
*.pdf   -text -diff
*.der   -text -diff
*.icc   -text -diff
*.jpeg  -text -diff
*.jpg   -text -diff
*.png   -text -diff
*.otf   -text -diff
*.ttf   -text -diff
